config BR2_PACKAGE_SINTY_BOARD_FIRMWARE
	bool "sinty-board-firmware"
	depends on BR2_aarch64
	help
	  UEFI firmware for boards that do not ship one, so they boot
	  the Sinty OS image like a PC: U-Boot with its EFI loader for
	  Jetson Nano, TX1 and TX2, EDK2 for Rock 5B and 5B+, and the
	  UEFI firmware for Raspberry Pi 4 and 5. The files land in
	  images/board-firmware, one folder per board.
